      },
      "hints": [
        "Use the two vectors from $F$ to $E$ and $D$; equivalently reverse both vectors found earlier.",
        "Dot $\\overrightarrow{EF}$ with $\\overrightarrow{DF}$ and divide by their moduli."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$\\overrightarrow{EF}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{DF}=(-6)(-6)+(-3)(0)+2(2)=40$.",
        "$|EF|=7$ and $|DF|=\\sqrt{(-6)^2+2^2}=\\sqrt{40}$. Thus $\\angle EFD=\\cos^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{40}{7\\sqrt{40}}\\right)=25.4^\\circ$."
